    "response": "Here’s a 4-day Iceland trip itinerary focused on nature and hot springs:\n\n### Day 1: Arrival and Hveravellir Hot Springs\n- **Morning**: Arrive in Iceland. Rent a car for easy travel.\n- **Afternoon**: Head to **Hveravellir**, a stunning geothermal area with hot springs.\n  - **Location**: Hveravellir, Hveravallavegur, Húnavatnssýsla, Iceland.\n  - Activities: Explore the unique geothermal features and enjoy a dip in the hot springs.\n- **Evening**: Stay overnight near Hveravellir, enjoy a local meal.\n\n### Day 2: Explore Nature at Langjökull and Nearby Hot Springs\n- **Morning**: Visit **Langjökull**, the second-largest glacier in Iceland.\n  - **Location**: Langjökull, Iceland.\n  - Activities: Take a glacier hike or join a guided tour.\n- **Afternoon**: After exploring Langjökull, relax at the nearby **Óskurhóll** hot springs.\n  - **Location**: Óskurhóll, Kjalvegur, Húnavatnssýsla, Iceland.\n- **Evening**: Return to your accommodation for dinner and rest.\n\n### Day 3: Scenic Views and Other Hot Springs\n- **Morning**: Visit **Mannabeinavatn**, a serene lake surrounded by beautiful landscapes.\n  - **Location**: Mannabeinavatn, Húnavatnssýsla, Iceland.\n- **Afternoon**: Go to **Bláhver**, a lovely hot spring area.\n  - **Location**: Bláhver, Kjalvegur, Húnavatnssýsla, Iceland.\n- **Evening**: Return to your accommodation or seek lodging near Bláhver. Enjoy local cuisine.\n\n### Day 4: Additional Nature Stops and Departure\n- **Morning**: Take a trip to **Djápagilsvatn**, known for its stunning views.\n  - **Location**: Djápagilsvatn, Skagafjörður, Iceland.\n- **Early Afternoon**: Head to **Eyvindarhver**, a lesser-known hot spring spot.\n  - **Location**: Eyvindarhver, Kjalvegur, Húnavatnssýsla, Iceland.\n- **Evening**: Depart from Iceland with unforgettable memories of nature and relaxation.\n\n### Tips\n- **Clothing**: Dress in layers and be prepared for rapidly changing weather.\n- **Driving**: Check road conditions, especially in winter.\n- **Reservations**: Make accommodation bookings in advance, especially in popular areas. \n\nEnjoy your trip filled with stunning natural beauty and relaxing hot springs!",
